<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Curtatone and Montanara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Curtatone and Montanara was fought on 29 May 1848 near Mantua, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italian-war-of-independence">First Italian War of Independence</a>. About 5,000 Tuscan and Neapolitan troops, including volunteer battalions of students and professors from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> and Siena, held off a much larger Austrian army under Radetzky for a day before retreating. Their resistance delayed the Austrians and helped the Piedmontese win at Goito the next day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-curtatone-and-montanara.jpg" alt="Battle of Curtatone and Montanara" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cesare Morbio (1812-1887) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Un_episodio_della_Battaglia_di_Novara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
